# EmailJS credentials — get these free at https://www.emailjs.com
# 1. Create an account, add an Email Service (e.g. Gmail) connected to sumitback1@gmail.com
# 2. Create an Email Template with variables: {{from_name}}, {{reply_to}}, {{message}}, {{subject}}, {{to_email}}
#    Set the template's "Subject" field to {{subject}} and "To email" to {{to_email}}
# 3. Copy the IDs below into a real .env file (never commit .env)

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_service_id
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_template_id
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key
